\fBbrowser\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH "H5I BROWSER START"
Start a browser session and print its id
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\fR [\fB\-\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-loopback\fR] [\fB\-\-script\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-\-height\fR] [\fB\-\-expires\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-restore\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIURL\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-in\fR \fI<BOX>\fR
Run the session inside this box instead of on this machine.

The box must already exist (`h5i box`) and be pinned to the `h5i\-light` engine. Its egress allowlist is enforced at the box\*(Aqs boundary, so the session\*(Aqs request lane becomes host\-observed.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\fR \fI<ORIGIN>\fR
Grant an origin. Repeatable. Without any, nothing remote is reachable except the URL\*(Aqs own origin
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-loopback\fR
Refuse loopback too. It is reachable by default: it is the dev server
.TP
\fB\-\-script\fR
Run the page\*(Aqs own JavaScript. Off by default: with script off, page\-borne prompt injection has no delivery channel at all
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<WIDTH>\fR [default: 1280]
Viewport width
.TP
\fB\-\-height\fR \fI<HEIGHT>\fR [default: 720]
Viewport height
.TP
\fB\-\-expires\-in\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
End the session automatically after this many seconds.

Recorded as an ending on the session\*(Aqs record when it passes, not as a disappearance: `h5i browser status` still answers afterwards, and says it expired.
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\fR \fI<SESSION>\fR
Seed this session\*(Aqs storage from one that has ended.

A restore is a **new session with a new id**, and the inheritance is written into its record. Nothing resurrects an id: an agent holding a stale one always gets a refusal, never a different session wearing the same name.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the session record as JSON instead of a summary line
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>
A URL, or a path to a local HTML file
